# A settings row's choice chips are click targets in their own right: a
# click on `on` sets the row to `on`, not merely focuses it. At 120x40
# the box spans x=24..95 and is centred vertically: under the box's
# section strip, `Relative line numbers` is row 11, its `[off]` chip
# starts at x=63 and the `on` chip at x=71.
command view.settings
expect screen contains "Relative line numbers:             [off] / on"
click 72 11
expect screen contains "Relative line numbers:             off / [on]"
click 64 11
expect screen contains "Relative line numbers:             [off] / on"
